# `Set` — no duplicates

## Membership, not position

```java
Set<String> tags = new HashSet<>();
tags.add("java");
tags.add("java");        // ignored — already present
tags.contains("java");   // true, and fast
```

`add` returns `true` if the element was **new** → detect first-seen in one step.

## "Same" = `equals` + `hashCode`

A `HashSet<Point>` dedups correctly **only if `Point` overrides `equals`/`hashCode`** (→ use records). Default identity `equals` → nothing looks duplicate.

## Three impls — pick by order

- **`HashSet`** — default, **no order**, O(1)
- **`LinkedHashSet`** — **insertion order**
- **`TreeSet`** — **sorted**, O(log n), range queries (`ceiling`, `floor`); uses `compareTo`, not `equals`

## Set algebra

```java
a.addAll(b);      // union
a.retainAll(b);   // intersection
a.removeAll(b);   // difference
```
